From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:05:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: App Control Center, Freezer and Student mode; no App
 lock

Mobile Manager pages on the 1204 model (MOBILE_MANAGER_APP_CONTROLS_UX):

* App Control Center (Mobile Manager, org.sableos.settings.APP_CONTROLS):
  every launcher app, plus apps the Freezer hid, with network access
  (the Network Manager's POLICY_REJECT_ALL view), background mode
  (Android's battery optimization mode) and paused state (Frozen,
  Student mode, Focus mode, or another app). Filters: all, network
  blocked or limited, background restricted, paused, frozen, hidden.
  Enter on an app: Freeze/Unfreeze, Hide/Show in launcher, Network
  access, App security & privacy, App info. Android's dialog for an app
  Settings paused now opens this page at that app.
* Freezer: one switch per app; frozen apps are suspended with
  setPackagesSuspended until unfrozen (data kept). Frozen apps the user
  installed can be hidden from the launcher with Android's per-user
  hidden setting; Settings only unhides what it hid, and unfreezing
  shows the app again. Apps the phone needs are never frozen.
* Student mode (org.sableos.settings.STUDENT_MODE), built on Focus
  mode: a second Settings-owned AutomaticZenRule with the same
  notification policy (so it is in Modes and Quick Settings), an allow
  list and a time window (days, start, end, default weekdays
  08:00-17:00, off until chosen). While on, every launcher app not
  allowed is paused. Settings keeps the window: an exact alarm at the
  next boundary, re-armed on boot and clock or time zone changes
  (SableStudentModeReceiver). Turning it off by hand lasts until the
  next boundary. Local control, not parental control; no site filter.
* SableAppSuspender is now the one place that suspends: Freezer,
  Student and Focus share Android's single suspension per suspender,
  so a mode ending never unfreezes an app. One dialog for all three,
  whose button opens the App Control Center.
* App lock is removed (page, rows, search entries): LineageOS 23.2 has
  no launch gate, so nothing claims protection it does not give.
  "app lock" searches land on Private Space & Dual Apps.
* Mobile Manager is also in Privacy & security (Safety Center's "More
  security & privacy" and the Privacy page), not indexed twice.
